# rtl8xxxu on the RTOS line, C3: the RTL8188EUS (0bda:8179) enumerates behind
# the external hub on the bench's "xhci0" - the GT kernel's xhci-hcd.0.auto,
# the DWC3 at 0xFCC00000, i.e. this board map's busid 3 - the vendored driver
# probes it over the linuxkpi USB engine, downloads rtlwifi/rtl8188eufw.bin from
# the compiled-in registry and registers its wiphy with the real mac80211;
# opening the interface reaches the driver's start.
#
# The controller list is a bench fact of this round: the user's 2026-11-14 setup
# put the dongle on a hub at xhci0, so the xHCI pair (busids 3,2) is the list and
# bus 3 is the one the claim line must name.  The case prints the list it tried
# and the claim hook prints bus/hub/port, so a moved dongle reads as evidence,
# not as a silent timeout.  EHCI (busids 1,0) stays a different profile/arm.
#
# The driver is GPL-2.0-only and the stack is GPL-2.0-only; this image is a
# GPL-2.0 link product that also redistributes the Realtek rtl8188eu firmware
# image (docs/LICENSES.md).

CONFIG_BACKEND_FREERTOS=y
CONFIG_OPT_O2=y
CONFIG_PROFILE_BASE=y
CONFIG_CASES="tick rtl8xxxu_c3"
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_PCI=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_SDIO=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_USB=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_CFG80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_MAC80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_RTL8XXXU=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_NET_NONE=y
CONFIG_FREERTOS_HEAP_SIZE=16777216
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SIZE=32768
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SLOTS=16
CONFIG_RTL8XXXU_USB_BUS=0
